    "summary": "Ice-scratcher, consisting of an ivory handle carved with a linked seal head, from a single piece of tusk, three bearded [?] seal claws, attached with a binding of plaited sinew tied through two holes in the underside of the scratcher. The seal head is detailed with inlaid balene or wood eyes, and carved muzzle. The back of the scratcher is incised with a geometric design in three parts, lines two for each claw, and a dashed line at the proximal end.",
